  "final_answer": "Done. Audit run as of 2026-03-31 against INT-09 rev 4. All four files written to `/app` and confirmed present.\n\n**Batch (28 audited requests, 8 accounts; 4 withdrawn excluded):** 14 flagged, 14 clean, 23 findings raised. Character 6, background 5, consent 3, commercial 6, disclosure 3. Escalated accounts 4 (ACC-02, ACC-03, ACC-07, ACC-08).\n\n**Things most worth your time before Thursday:**\n- Two findings turn on **supersessions that narrowed scope** \u2014 LIC-109 cut the Rook & Raven character cap 35%\u219220% (biting REQ-05 at 28.7%), and LIC-110 cut the Old Quarry Skyline background scope `all`\u2192`print_for_sale` (biting REQ-28's personal_only use, while REQ-18 stayed covered). These are the cases likely to be queried.\n- Two `COMMERCIAL_DISTRIBUTION_FLAG` findings (REQ-14, REQ-30) rest on **lapsed agreements** (ACC-04, ACC-08) whose recorded coverage clears nothing; reinstating either flips those two.\n- \u00a78 split: ACC-02 and ACC-03 escalate on the 3-finding limb (REQ-05, REQ-10), ACC-07 and ACC-08 on share > batch (66.7% vs 50.0%). Five accounts sit exactly on the batch share and do not escalate on the first limb.\n\nThe memo stands on its own and names the deciding record (licence / consent / agreement) for every finding, plus every cleared false-positive the numbers would otherwise read as a breach.",
